259
00:10:51,064 --> 00:10:52,094
(Everyone is so deep into their jjamppong.)

260
00:10:52,094 --> 00:10:54,104
Tangsuyuk got a little cold.

261
00:10:54,104 --> 00:10:55,134
A moment ago...

262
00:10:55,204 --> 00:10:56,634
(I forgot about the tangsuyuk.)

263
00:10:56,804 --> 00:10:59,904
- The feeling of the first bite...
- It's really good.

264
00:10:59,904 --> 00:11:01,004
(Without hesitation, they go for the next target.)

265
00:11:01,004 --> 00:11:02,004
It's still good.

266
00:11:02,004 --> 00:11:03,074
(It's tangsuyuk.)

267
00:11:03,814 --> 00:11:05,574
(She takes a bite even before sitting back down.)

268
00:11:05,574 --> 00:11:06,574
(Humming)

269
00:11:06,574 --> 00:11:07,614
(Nodding)

270
00:11:08,314 --> 00:11:14,024
(At the end of every set of chopsticks)

271
00:11:15,154 --> 00:11:20,694
(A beautifully glazed piece of tangsuyuk)

272
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,964
(The sweet and sticky sauce stretches out.)

273
00:11:24,564 --> 00:11:25,964
- Isn't it good?
- It tastes so good.

274
00:11:26,294 --> 00:11:27,964
It's perfectly fried.

275
00:11:27,964 --> 00:11:29,004
- Isn't it?
- Seriously.

276
00:11:29,004 --> 00:11:30,774
- Right.
- The tangsuyuk is well fried.

277
00:11:30,774 --> 00:11:32,304
- I agree.
- It's incredible.

278
00:11:32,304 --> 00:11:33,334
It's well fried.

279
00:11:34,604 --> 00:11:36,644
Ever since I made that mistake...

280
00:11:36,644 --> 00:11:37,674
(Overcoming the trauma of the past)

281
00:11:37,674 --> 00:11:40,144
- I never forget 170°C.
- I see.

282
00:11:40,144 --> 00:11:42,244
When the oil hits 170°C,

283
00:11:42,244 --> 00:11:43,284
I put in the meat.

284
00:11:43,414 --> 00:11:46,314
You completely mastered how to cook tangsuyuk.

285
00:11:46,314 --> 00:11:47,524
(Feeling proud)

286
00:11:47,984 --> 00:11:49,324
And pepper japchae.

287
00:11:49,324 --> 00:11:50,924
(All right, let's try some pepper japchae.)

288
00:11:51,094 --> 00:11:52,254
Pepper japchae?

289
00:11:52,254 --> 00:11:53,864
(They're busy eating so much food.)

290
00:11:54,094 --> 00:11:56,864
(As Jung Ah said, he grabs a handful of pepper japchae.)

291
00:11:57,864 --> 00:11:59,034
(Crunchy)

292
00:11:59,034 --> 00:12:00,134
- It's a little spicy.
- Really?

293
00:12:00,334 --> 00:12:01,434
I like spicy food.

294
00:12:01,434 --> 00:12:02,564
(The spicy kick spreads with every chew.)

295
00:12:02,564 --> 00:12:03,604
It's delicious.

296
00:12:04,774 --> 00:12:05,874
It has a lot of vegetables.

297
00:12:05,874 --> 00:12:07,144
(Tender meat, crisp vegetables)

298
00:12:07,144 --> 00:12:08,174
It's so good.

299
00:12:08,174 --> 00:12:09,874
(The siblings' pepper japchae)

300
00:12:09,944 --> 00:12:11,444
- Can you give me a flower bun?
- Sure.

301
00:12:11,744 --> 00:12:13,684
- I should try some.
- Here you go.

302
00:12:13,684 --> 00:12:15,344
(For glossy pepper japchae, )

303
00:12:15,684 --> 00:12:17,414
(fluffy flower buns are a must.)

304
00:12:17,954 --> 00:12:19,314
(Pile a generous handful onto the flower bun)

305
00:12:19,314 --> 00:12:20,484
It's like we're in a fairy tale.

306
00:12:21,124 --> 00:12:24,524
(Wrap it up at the perfect golden ratio)

307
00:12:25,154 --> 00:12:27,424
(After one juicy, fluffy bite)

308
00:12:28,924 --> 00:12:30,664
(A pepper japchae wrap is born automatically.)

309
00:12:30,664 --> 00:12:31,664
Pepper japchae?

310
00:12:32,534 --> 00:12:33,904
Why is it so spicy?

311
00:12:34,364 --> 00:12:35,704
That's why it's so good.

312
00:12:36,134 --> 00:12:37,674
Smashed cucumber salad goes well with spicy food.

313
00:12:37,674 --> 00:12:40,874
(A fresh smashed cucumber salad awaits.)

314
00:12:41,374 --> 00:12:43,844
(With one slice of crunchy cucumber, )

315
00:12:44,174 --> 00:12:45,844
(it starts again.)

316
00:12:45,844 --> 00:12:48,014
- That's why it's so good.
- It's really nice.

317
00:12:48,014 --> 00:12:51,554
(Jjamppong, tangsuyuk, pepper japchae)

318
00:12:51,714 --> 00:12:54,084
(The siblings' infinite food loop)

319
00:12:54,084 --> 00:12:55,754
- I feel so happy.
- I'm really happy.

320
00:12:55,754 --> 00:12:56,824
Right now,

321
00:12:57,124 --> 00:12:59,024
it's 8pm, but it's still bright outside.

322
00:12:59,694 --> 00:13:01,764
- It's beautiful back there.
- The view is so pretty.

323
00:13:01,764 --> 00:13:03,734
- The view is incredible.
- I know.

324
00:13:03,934 --> 00:13:05,564
It's like we're shooting "Country Diaries."

325
00:13:06,264 --> 00:13:07,434
- Right?
- Yes.

326
00:13:07,434 --> 00:13:09,204
- This is insane.
- I feel so happy.

327
00:13:09,204 --> 00:13:10,734
Look at the scenery.

328
00:13:10,804 --> 00:13:12,134
It looks like a TV drama set.

329
00:13:12,134 --> 00:13:13,604
The weather is beautiful too.

330
00:13:13,744 --> 00:13:15,044
This is amazing.

331
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,844
(The sunset shimmers across the waves.)

332
00:13:18,874 --> 00:13:22,144
(As the day comes to an end, the sun heads home to rest.)

333
00:13:23,414 --> 00:13:26,754
(The Siblings' House beneath the legendary West Coast sunset)

334
00:13:27,154 --> 00:13:28,924
This place is really beautiful.

335
00:13:28,924 --> 00:13:29,954
(The food is delicious, and the scenery is beautiful.)

336
00:13:29,954 --> 00:13:32,994
How did they even find a place like this?

337
00:13:33,454 --> 00:13:34,564
(The siblings are busy eating and enjoying the view.)

338
00:13:34,564 --> 00:13:36,464
- It's so beautiful.
- It's like we're in a fairy tale.

339
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:40,464
Jung Ah, how can you make all this food?

340
00:13:40,534 --> 00:13:41,534
- I know.
- I know.

341
00:13:41,534 --> 00:13:43,164
I heard that you didn't cook until a few years ago.

342
00:13:44,334 --> 00:13:45,634
- I learned how to cook.
- No.

343
00:13:45,634 --> 00:13:48,574
If Jung Ah doesn't cook at home,

344
00:13:48,574 --> 00:13:49,604
she can't cook this well.

345
00:13:49,604 --> 00:13:51,674
- She must cook every day.
- Right.

346
00:13:52,244 --> 00:13:55,084
Have you made jjamppong at home?

347
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:56,084
Just once.

348
00:13:56,084 --> 00:13:57,954
(You made jjamppong at home?)

349
00:13:57,954 --> 00:13:59,014
Seriously?

350
00:14:01,724 --> 00:14:03,384
Try this.

351
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:04,794
(This was a good meal.)

352
00:14:04,794 --> 00:14:07,164
(Manila clams)

353
00:14:07,164 --> 00:14:08,194
(Nodding)

354
00:14:08,194 --> 00:14:09,424
All that hard work paid off.

355
00:14:10,834 --> 00:14:12,164
My goodness.

356
00:14:12,164 --> 00:14:13,464
(We gave it everything we had.)

357
00:14:13,464 --> 00:14:14,934
Today's Manila Clam Festival was great.

358
00:14:14,934 --> 00:14:16,464
- It was great.
- Manila Clam Festival was amazing.

359
00:14:16,464 --> 00:14:17,474
(Today's Manila Clam Festival was great.)

360
00:14:17,474 --> 00:14:18,674
- Seriously, - Seriously.

361
00:14:18,674 --> 00:14:20,204
starting with Cho Jung Seok's appearance...

362
00:14:20,204 --> 00:14:21,604
I know.

363
00:14:22,044 --> 00:14:23,744
The real thrill ended right there.

364
00:14:23,744 --> 00:14:25,774
- Right.
- "Is Cho Jung Seok coming?"

365
00:14:25,774 --> 00:14:27,244
- Even now...
- Underneath

366
00:14:27,244 --> 00:14:30,854
(Singing as a response even though it's late)

367
00:14:30,954 --> 00:14:32,814
How about a round of Balance Game?

368
00:14:33,624 --> 00:14:36,954
Getting kidnapped by your current husband...

369
00:14:36,954 --> 00:14:40,054
versus getting kidnapped by some random stranger.

370
00:14:41,264 --> 00:14:42,364
(It's an absurd choice to make.)

371
00:14:42,364 --> 00:14:43,394
Obviously, I'd choose my husband.

372
00:14:44,164 --> 00:14:46,494
- A stranger would be scary.
- Right.

373
00:14:47,004 --> 00:14:48,264
How about you, Jung Seok?

374
00:14:49,234 --> 00:14:50,304
Me?

375
00:14:50,504 --> 00:14:52,704
I'll say the same thing.

376
00:14:52,704 --> 00:14:53,704
(Current wife versus a stranger)

377
00:14:53,704 --> 00:14:55,244
Obviously, I'd pick Gummy. I'm her husband.

378
00:14:55,244 --> 00:14:56,274
He's Gummy's husband.

379
00:14:57,014 --> 00:14:58,374
- Ask me to choose...
- Yes?

380
00:14:58,374 --> 00:14:59,974
- between my current husband...
- Yes.

381
00:14:59,974 --> 00:15:02,314
and Matt Damon.

382
00:15:02,684 --> 00:15:04,914
- She must like Matt Damon.
- Matt Damon is so handsome.

383
00:15:05,184 --> 00:15:07,854
- He really is.
- Kidnapped by your husband...

384
00:15:07,854 --> 00:15:09,584
- or by Matt Damon.
- Matt Damon.

385
00:15:09,584 --> 00:15:11,294
I'd definitely choose Matt Damon.

386
00:15:11,294 --> 00:15:12,554
(Matt Damon's name echoes across Taean.)

387
00:15:12,554 --> 00:15:14,564
Getting kidnapped by your current husband...

388
00:15:14,564 --> 00:15:15,764
or getting kidnapped by a wild boar?

389
00:15:15,764 --> 00:15:16,764
A wild boar?

390
00:15:17,494 --> 00:15:18,634
(Laughing)

391
00:15:18,634 --> 00:15:20,334
- What's wrong with him?
- What?

392
00:15:20,334 --> 00:15:22,404
Getting kidnapped by your current husband...

393
00:15:22,534 --> 00:15:23,674
or kidnapping Matt Damon.

394
00:15:24,904 --> 00:15:27,704
I prefer to kidnap Matt Damon.

395
00:15:27,704 --> 00:15:28,874
(Matt Damon: I'm doomed.)

396
00:15:28,874 --> 00:15:30,004
Why do you like him so much?

397
00:15:30,544 --> 00:15:31,614
Are you happy just imagining it?

398
00:15:31,814 --> 00:15:34,014
Balance Game is fun sometimes.

399
00:15:34,014 --> 00:15:35,184
(Proud creator of the world's most hopeless Balance Game)

400
00:15:35,584 --> 00:15:36,644
(Enough with this messed up Balance Game)

401
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:37,854
You're one step ahead.

402
00:15:38,114 --> 00:15:39,254
This is crazy.

403
00:15:39,314 --> 00:15:41,024
Should we talk about tomorrow's schedule?

404
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:42,224
- Yes.
- That sounds good.

405
00:15:42,654 --> 00:15:44,694
- It's gotten very hot.
- Yes.

406
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:47,894
For tomorrow's work, you'll start early...

407
00:15:47,894 --> 00:15:49,664
before the sun gets too hot.

408
00:15:50,164 --> 00:15:52,594
You'll leave here tomorrow at 7:30am.

409
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:54,734
- At 7:30am?
- Leave here at 7:30am?

410
00:15:55,534 --> 00:15:57,834
It's not the sea tomorrow, right?

411
00:15:57,834 --> 00:16:00,444
Can you at least tell us where we're going?

412
00:16:00,444 --> 00:16:02,004
Just tell us if it's on land or on land.

413
00:16:02,004 --> 00:16:04,444
It has to be on land.

414
00:16:04,444 --> 00:16:06,144
- "On land or on land?"
- On land.

415
00:16:06,244 --> 00:16:08,014
- It can't be the sea again.
- On land...

416
00:16:08,014 --> 00:16:10,114
Tell us if it's on land or at the sea.

417
00:16:10,484 --> 00:16:12,184
Tell us if it's the sea or the river.

418
00:16:12,184 --> 00:16:13,724
(Jung Seok wants to know if it's the sea or the river.)

419
00:16:13,724 --> 00:16:15,824
You'll be working with us tomorrow, right?

420
00:16:15,824 --> 00:16:17,354
- Will you work with us?
- I...

421
00:16:17,924 --> 00:16:19,194
(Tomorrow as well?)

422
00:16:19,554 --> 00:16:21,624
- Of course. I'm a member too.
- Once you're done working,

423
00:16:21,624 --> 00:16:22,864
we'll send you home.

424
00:16:22,864 --> 00:16:25,094
- Sure.
- You should work with us.

425
00:16:25,094 --> 00:16:26,194
(Planning to let him leave when it's time for his other schedule)

426
00:16:26,194 --> 00:16:27,834
Without coming back home.

427
00:16:27,834 --> 00:16:28,964
- Will he leave after that?
- Without coming back here?

428
00:16:29,604 --> 00:16:30,774
(That's so sad.)

429
00:16:30,774 --> 00:16:32,304
Are you leaving?

430
00:16:32,534 --> 00:16:34,004
How about being the 1st to work 3 days?

431
00:16:34,204 --> 00:16:35,874
That's a bit...

432
00:16:36,004 --> 00:16:37,144
He has a shoot tomorrow.

433
00:16:37,144 --> 00:16:38,414
- If he didn't have a shoot...
- Go to the shoot...

434
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,674
and come back at night.

435
00:16:39,674 --> 00:16:40,884
I'll be waiting for you.

436
00:16:41,284 --> 00:16:42,914
- I'll be waiting for you.
- Really?

437
00:16:42,914 --> 00:16:44,684
I'll have the blankets laid out and wait for you.

438
00:16:44,684 --> 00:16:47,224
All right. In that case...

439
00:16:47,854 --> 00:16:49,124
"Have the blankets laid out?"

440
00:16:49,124 --> 00:16:50,424
(Why would you have the blankets laid out?)

441
00:16:51,024 --> 00:16:53,224
(I can't stay here, but...)

442
00:16:53,224 --> 00:16:55,024
I'll give you a personal call.

443
00:16:56,524 --> 00:16:58,134
- "Be quiet."
- To let him know his plans.

444
00:16:58,134 --> 00:16:59,534
(Jung Seok reached his limit.)

445
00:16:59,534 --> 00:17:01,034
Is it around 9pm?

446
00:17:01,034 --> 00:17:03,634
- It's 8pm.
- It's 8:20pm.

447
00:17:03,634 --> 00:17:04,634
It's 8:20pm.

448
00:17:04,634 --> 00:17:06,434
- Let's prepare drinks and snacks.
- Okay.

449
00:17:06,434 --> 00:17:07,974
I'll clean up here.

450
00:17:07,974 --> 00:17:09,044
You guys go and prepare drinks and snacks.

451
00:17:09,204 --> 00:17:10,974
- We'll clean up here.
- Jung Ah, get some rest.

452
00:17:11,144 --> 00:17:12,974
- Hold on.
- I'm sorry.

453
00:17:12,974 --> 00:17:14,244
- Give me the leftovers.
- Isn't that better?

454
00:17:14,414 --> 00:17:15,414
(He takes the leftover dishes back.)

455
00:17:15,414 --> 00:17:16,944
- I'm sorry.
- Let me have some more.

456
00:17:16,944 --> 00:17:18,414
- I'm not done eating.
- Stay seated.

457
00:17:18,414 --> 00:17:20,214
Do you want another drink?

458
00:17:20,214 --> 00:17:21,384
No, it's okay.

459
00:17:21,384 --> 00:17:22,624
(One more piece...)

460
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,454
(and another)

461
00:17:24,454 --> 00:17:25,854
Let's put on some pain patches.

462
00:17:25,854 --> 00:17:27,294
(Chewing endlessly)

463
00:17:27,294 --> 00:17:28,324
Yoon Seo.

464
00:17:30,194 --> 00:17:31,564
(She spots him.)

465
00:17:31,564 --> 00:17:32,634
Stop eating.

466
00:17:33,064 --> 00:17:34,134
Stop eating.

467
00:17:34,134 --> 00:17:35,134
(Smashing his thigh)

468
00:17:35,134 --> 00:17:36,464
- Why?
- No.

469
00:17:36,464 --> 00:17:38,534
You'll be going on a diet as soon as you leave.

470
00:17:40,004 --> 00:17:41,774
You should've made it less delicious.

471
00:17:41,774 --> 00:17:43,174
It's so good that I can't stop.

472
00:17:44,814 --> 00:17:46,774
I lost my control as soon as I saw the jjamppong.

473
00:17:46,974 --> 00:17:48,844
This is insanely good.

474
00:17:49,544 --> 00:17:50,854
The day goes by so fast.

475
00:17:51,314 --> 00:17:53,414
- Let's clean up now.
- Okay.

476
00:17:53,414 --> 00:17:54,454
Shall we?

477
00:17:55,654 --> 00:17:58,594
(With everyone helping out, the table is cleared in no time.)

478
00:17:58,854 --> 00:18:00,154
- Did you wipe it already?
- What?

479
00:18:00,154 --> 00:18:01,724
- Yes, I wiped it.
- I'll take it inside.

480
00:18:01,724 --> 00:18:02,794
(You Seok helps Yoon Seo who's clearing the table.)

481
00:18:04,134 --> 00:18:06,664
- Give it to me.
- You can't carry both at once.

482
00:18:06,964 --> 00:18:08,064
I'm a man.

483
00:18:08,064 --> 00:18:09,204
(Groaning)

484
00:18:09,764 --> 00:18:12,504
(A terrifying comment for the little sister)

485
00:18:12,504 --> 00:18:14,744
(She runs away immediately.)

486
00:18:15,004 --> 00:18:16,704
(However...)

487
00:18:16,704 --> 00:18:17,974
I don't think you can carry it.

488
00:18:18,714 --> 00:18:20,414
- This...
- Give it to me.

489
00:18:20,414 --> 00:18:21,614
- Be careful.
- It's fine.

490
00:18:21,614 --> 00:18:24,054
- Hey, I'm a man.
- Take on what you can handle.

491
00:18:24,054 --> 00:18:26,084
(Laughing)

492
00:18:26,614 --> 00:18:27,824
This is nothing.

493
00:18:27,924 --> 00:18:29,384
Your face is very red.

494
00:18:29,384 --> 00:18:31,224
(In the end, the man cleared both tables.)

495
00:18:31,754 --> 00:18:32,754
How shall we do this?

496
00:18:32,754 --> 00:18:34,464
The ladies should wash up first.

497
00:18:34,464 --> 00:18:36,094
Then I'll go after Jung Ah.

498
00:18:36,194 --> 00:18:38,134
Jung Ah, you worked hard today.

499
00:18:38,194 --> 00:18:40,334
- Are you having a good time?
- Yes, it's a lot of fun.

500
00:18:40,334 --> 00:18:42,864
- I like variety shows like this.
- I see.

501
00:18:43,434 --> 00:18:46,034
(Under the dim lights)

502
00:18:46,034 --> 00:18:47,034
(Giggling)

503
00:18:47,544 --> 00:18:48,844
Did you have fun again today?

504
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,144
Yes, but it was hard today.

505
00:18:51,374 --> 00:18:52,514
Was harvesting Manila clams hard?

506
00:18:52,514 --> 00:18:54,384
It was like doing Pilates.

507
00:18:54,814 --> 00:18:57,614
If harvesting wild rock seaweed was a personal training session,

508
00:18:57,784 --> 00:19:00,114
- this time felt more like Pilates.
- That's an accurate comparison.

509
00:19:00,554 --> 00:19:01,854
I'm done washing up.

510
00:19:01,984 --> 00:19:03,054
Okay.

511
00:19:03,454 --> 00:19:06,754
- Well done.
- Thank you.

512
00:19:06,794 --> 00:19:08,194
Who's going next?

513
00:19:08,364 --> 00:19:10,164
It's me, Jong Seok.

514
00:19:10,164 --> 00:19:11,764
- Jong Seok.
- Jong Seok.

515
00:19:11,764 --> 00:19:13,234
- Jong Seok.
- He's next.

516
00:19:13,434 --> 00:19:15,964
We have to hear Jong Seok sing.

517
00:19:16,064 --> 00:19:17,164
- Really?
- I'd love to hear him sing...

518
00:19:17,164 --> 00:19:19,734
his new song while playing the guitar.

519
00:19:19,734 --> 00:19:21,204
I can't play the guitar for the new song.

520
00:19:21,204 --> 00:19:22,504
- You can't?
- No.

521
00:19:22,504 --> 00:19:23,844
It won't work.

522
00:19:23,844 --> 00:19:26,074
- Then I will.
- Will you sing a song?

523
00:19:26,074 --> 00:19:27,484
Yes, I know how to play the guitar.

524
00:19:27,484 --> 00:19:29,714
- Do you know how to play it?
- You can play the guitar?

525
00:19:29,714 --> 00:19:31,654
- Of course.
- That's amazing.

526
00:19:31,654 --> 00:19:32,754
How so?

527
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:34,484
- I can't wait to hear it.
- I can't play the guitar.

528
00:19:35,024 --> 00:19:36,284
Let's hear it.

529
00:19:36,284 --> 00:19:40,894
(Everyone holds their breath to hear her performance.)

530
00:19:40,894 --> 00:19:42,294
She knows how to play it.

531
00:19:44,564 --> 00:19:46,094
I'd like to do it, but I don't remember it.

532
00:19:46,094 --> 00:19:47,764
(This time, Yoon Seo goes up to the piano.)

533
00:19:47,764 --> 00:19:49,504
Yoon Seo, play the piano.

534
00:19:49,504 --> 00:19:52,134
That's good. That's it.

535
00:19:52,674 --> 00:19:55,174
- Yoon Seo is...
- That's amazing.

536
00:19:55,174 --> 00:19:56,204
Yoon Seo.

537
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,474
- Do you want to play together?
- This is all I know.

538
00:19:58,474 --> 00:20:00,114
This is the only thing I can play.

539
00:20:00,114 --> 00:20:02,044
(A band forms at the speed of light.)

540
00:20:02,444 --> 00:20:04,314
- Start.
- Start.

541
00:20:04,314 --> 00:20:06,484
(The jam session begins just as quickly.)

542
00:20:06,784 --> 00:20:09,024
(Whatever the siblings want to play)

543
00:20:09,024 --> 00:20:11,024
(Clunk, clunk)

544
00:20:11,654 --> 00:20:15,994
("Even dissonance counts as harmony" by Siblings Band)

545
00:20:16,464 --> 00:20:17,994
(Pitch: 0, Rhythm: Minus 2, Fun: 100)

546
00:20:17,994 --> 00:20:19,694
Jung Ah, how was our jam session?

547
00:20:20,364 --> 00:20:21,504
It was excellent.

548
00:20:21,504 --> 00:20:24,104
- While wearing a sheet mask...
- Goodness.

549
00:20:24,104 --> 00:20:25,874
- That was fun.
- It was hilarious.

550
00:20:26,774 --> 00:20:29,404
- Only with my right hand...
- I'm sorry.

551
00:20:31,114 --> 00:20:32,844
- This is...
- Yes, that's it.

552
00:20:32,844 --> 00:20:35,014
(He demonstrates how to play the classical guitar.)

553
00:20:35,014 --> 00:20:37,114
The touch is completely different.

554
00:20:37,114 --> 00:20:39,214
- It sounds lovely.
- It's different.

555
00:20:39,214 --> 00:20:41,384
- He's really good at it.
- It's so sad.

556
00:20:41,384 --> 00:20:44,694
- Would you play a duet with me?
- A duet?

557
00:20:44,694 --> 00:20:46,454
How about playing "Spring in My Hometown?"

558
00:20:46,454 --> 00:20:49,594
- Goodness.
- Please, just once.

559
00:20:49,664 --> 00:20:51,964
- Sun Young, - Yes?

560
00:20:51,964 --> 00:20:54,064
could you play mi on the piano?

561
00:20:55,034 --> 00:20:56,204
That was sol.

562
00:20:56,204 --> 00:20:57,204
(Laughing)

563
00:20:57,204 --> 00:20:59,434
(That was sol.)

564
00:20:59,704 --> 00:21:00,774
(After glancing back at Jung Seok who's tuning his guitar)

565
00:21:00,774 --> 00:21:02,774
What kind of feeling should I play with?

566
00:21:03,274 --> 00:21:06,144
Something bluesy or sweet?

567
00:21:06,944 --> 00:21:08,884
Or should it feel more like a march?

568
00:21:08,884 --> 00:21:10,954
Whatever feeling you want is possible.

569
00:21:10,954 --> 00:21:12,984
Could you stay quiet...

570
00:21:12,984 --> 00:21:14,524
- I'll keep quiet.
- until I finish tuning?

571
00:21:14,524 --> 00:21:16,354
(A quiet feeling)

572
00:21:16,824 --> 00:21:18,624
(It's already funny.)

573
00:21:18,624 --> 00:21:20,024
Are you sensitive about tuning?

574
00:21:20,024 --> 00:21:21,394
- It's tuned.
- It's done.

575
00:21:21,394 --> 00:21:22,494
Let's start now.

576
00:21:22,494 --> 00:21:23,594
One, two.

577
00:21:25,134 --> 00:21:30,104
(Sun Young and Jung Seok's duet performance finally begins.)

578
00:21:30,104 --> 00:21:33,374
(Impressed)

579
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,444
(Swaying side to side to the rhythm)

580
00:21:37,744 --> 00:21:41,114
(After making eye contact, Jung Seok starts singing too.)

581
00:21:41,114 --> 00:21:43,944
(My, he's singing too!)

582
00:21:44,784 --> 00:21:48,554
(Everyone is locked in on their surprisingly solid performance.)

583
00:21:49,284 --> 00:21:50,424
Jung Ah, sing it.

584
00:21:50,424 --> 00:21:52,654
(Jung Ah, sing it!)

585
00:21:53,424 --> 00:21:56,594
(Jung Ah adds cute little moves to her singing!)

586
00:21:57,634 --> 00:22:03,904
(This performance will help them cherish their memories of Taean.)

587
00:22:04,104 --> 00:22:05,474
- You know...
- Right.

588
00:22:05,704 --> 00:22:08,174
- When will I get to do this again?
- Exactly.

589
00:22:09,144 --> 00:22:10,204
What do you mean I'm acting weird?

590
00:22:10,204 --> 00:22:12,414
- You're still being so shy.
- He just got out of the shower.

591
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:13,474
(You Seok is being so shy, and the older members find him cute.)

592
00:22:13,474 --> 00:22:14,914
I find it so adorable...

593
00:22:14,914 --> 00:22:16,314
- how he's been so quiet all day.
- Oh, today...

594
00:22:16,514 --> 00:22:18,554
- Seriously...
- I guess he's usually chatty.

595
00:22:18,554 --> 00:22:19,654
- Yes, he really is.
- But...

596
00:22:19,654 --> 00:22:21,184
he loosened up by dinner time.

597
00:22:21,184 --> 00:22:22,554
Usually, he won't stop talking...

598
00:22:22,554 --> 00:22:24,354
- when he's around us.
- Hey, You Seok.

599
00:22:24,354 --> 00:22:26,494
Were you really acting weird this morning...

600
00:22:26,494 --> 00:22:27,724
because of me?

601
00:22:28,364 --> 00:22:30,564
- Well, yes, it was because of you.
- It's understandable...

602
00:22:30,624 --> 00:22:33,834
But seriously... What... Why was it because of me?

603
00:22:33,834 --> 00:22:35,634
- It's because he was excited.
- Come on. What's wrong with you?

604
00:22:35,634 --> 00:22:37,804
- I mean... It's not like that.
- It's normal to freeze up...

605
00:22:37,804 --> 00:22:38,934
- when you meet someone you admire.
- Exactly.

606
00:22:38,934 --> 00:22:41,444
It's like when you have a huge crush on someone,

607
00:22:41,444 --> 00:22:43,704
- you get all awkward around her.
- You get all awkward.

608
00:22:43,704 --> 00:22:45,344
- You just freeze up.
- That's how I felt.

609
00:22:45,344 --> 00:22:47,584
You have such a great vibe, and you're so witty.

610
00:22:47,584 --> 00:22:49,184
You always bring laughter to everyone around you.

611
00:22:49,184 --> 00:22:50,954
I'm so jealous of all those amazing traits you have.

612
00:22:51,054 --> 00:22:53,684
I think you were born with those traits.

613
00:22:53,684 --> 00:22:55,084
- I agree.
- Yes, he was born with them.

614
00:22:55,084 --> 00:22:56,784
Whenever I see someone like you,

615
00:22:56,784 --> 00:22:59,554
- I'm amazed by your sense of humour.
- Right. He's adaptable, isn't he?

616
00:22:59,554 --> 00:23:01,864
- He's very adaptable.
- Yes, he's very adaptable.

617
00:23:01,864 --> 00:23:03,724
When we were chatting in the car,

618
00:23:04,094 --> 00:23:06,434
I was so impressed by his witty comebacks.

619
00:23:06,734 --> 00:23:08,504
- Those were so incredible.
- That's right. I mean...

620
00:23:08,504 --> 00:23:10,034
He responded so quickly and wittily.

621
00:23:11,104 --> 00:23:12,404
His jokes just blew my mind.

622
00:23:13,134 --> 00:23:14,374
- Come on. I'm not...
- I was like, "He's amazing."

623
00:23:14,374 --> 00:23:16,474
- I'm not that witty.
- "He's incredible."

624
00:23:16,474 --> 00:23:18,674
- Even when he's acting...
- "That was a good one."

625
00:23:19,044 --> 00:23:22,584
(They went on chatting and laughing for a while.)

626
00:23:22,744 --> 00:23:24,314
- Right?
- Gosh, she's driving me crazy.

627
00:23:24,314 --> 00:23:28,424
(Their first night in Taean deepened with a pleasant conversation.)

628
00:23:31,094 --> 00:23:34,894
(And a brand new day has dawned.)

629
00:23:35,394 --> 00:23:38,834
(Under the reddish glow of the sky, )

630
00:23:38,834 --> 00:23:41,904
(a brand new morning breaks in Taean.)

631
00:23:43,064 --> 00:23:48,344
(Small movements awaken the morning, )

632
00:23:49,074 --> 00:23:55,284
(and everyone slowly starts the day in their own way.)

633
00:23:56,644 --> 00:24:01,254
(How will the siblings' day unfold today?)

634
00:24:03,424 --> 00:24:04,424
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo woke up.)

635
00:24:04,424 --> 00:24:06,254
Jung Ah, did you sleep well?

636
00:24:07,624 --> 00:24:10,124
(They're overflowing with affection first thing in the morning.)

637
00:24:10,624 --> 00:24:12,464
(Kicking her feet)

638
00:24:13,364 --> 00:24:15,134
This blanket is so soft.

639
00:24:16,834 --> 00:24:18,304
(Hugging her affectionately)

640
00:24:18,774 --> 00:24:19,874
Go back to sleep.

641
00:24:20,274 --> 00:24:21,804
- Sleep for another ten minutes.
- Okay.

642
00:24:23,044 --> 00:24:27,144
(Jung Ah steps out with her work clothes.)

643
00:24:28,914 --> 00:24:29,914
(Groaning)

644
00:24:30,244 --> 00:24:32,384
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes, I did.

645
00:24:32,384 --> 00:24:34,154
- Jung Ah, good morning.
- Good morning.

646
00:24:35,584 --> 00:24:36,654
Jung Ah, I'll fold the bedding.

647
00:24:36,654 --> 00:24:38,294
You can go ahead and do your makeup. Please sit down.

648
00:24:39,454 --> 00:24:41,264
- Jung Ah.
- That's okay.

649
00:24:41,994 --> 00:24:44,094
It doesn't matter who folds the bedding.

650
00:24:44,094 --> 00:24:45,534
Don't worry about it.

651
00:24:45,934 --> 00:24:49,134
You see, I have something to ask you about,

652
00:24:49,234 --> 00:24:50,234
Village Chief.

653
00:24:50,664 --> 00:24:53,434
- Why am I the village chief?
- Then who else?

654
00:24:54,174 --> 00:24:56,804
You see... By the way...

655
00:24:57,374 --> 00:25:01,114
There's something I'm curious about.

656
00:25:01,884 --> 00:25:02,944
(Chuckling)

657
00:25:03,414 --> 00:25:05,984
- A skit first thing in the morning?
- I don't think they're up yet.

658
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:07,724
- Good morning.
- Did you sleep well, Jung Seok?

659
00:25:08,184 --> 00:25:09,654
Did you sleep well, Village Chief?

660
00:25:09,654 --> 00:25:12,294
- We never...
- Why am I the village chief?

661
00:25:12,294 --> 00:25:13,294
- Well...
- started a skit...

662
00:25:13,924 --> 00:25:16,194
I just heard her calling you "Village Chief."

663
00:25:16,194 --> 00:25:18,894
(The morning skit boosts their energy.)

664
00:25:19,594 --> 00:25:21,904
- Did you sleep well?
- Yes, I slept well.

665
00:25:21,904 --> 00:25:23,604
You set the alarm for 6:30am.

666
00:25:23,934 --> 00:25:25,404
- Did I?
- Yes.

667
00:25:26,304 --> 00:25:27,474
Why did I do that?

668
00:25:28,874 --> 00:25:30,044
Let's slather on plenty of sunscreen.

669
00:25:30,704 --> 00:25:33,114
- Slather on plenty of sunscreen.
- Plenty.

670
00:25:33,974 --> 00:25:35,514
(She gets fully geared up for today's unknown task.)

671
00:25:35,514 --> 00:25:37,014
It's an outfit for farm work.

672
00:25:38,354 --> 00:25:40,554
I'm all set.

673
00:25:43,824 --> 00:25:45,154
(All set)

674
00:25:45,154 --> 00:25:46,154
Let's go.

675
00:25:47,294 --> 00:25:48,594
- Let's go.
- Are we leaving now?

676
00:25:48,594 --> 00:25:50,194
- Are we leaving right away?
- Yes.

677
00:25:52,734 --> 00:25:54,334
I'm going to draw on my eyebrows,

678
00:25:54,334 --> 00:25:56,104
so please let me know when you stop the car.

679
00:25:56,334 --> 00:25:58,274
She always draws on her eyebrows in the car.

680
00:25:58,674 --> 00:26:01,174
(Checking her eyebrows)

681
00:26:01,644 --> 00:26:02,774
- Do my eyebrows look okay?
- Oh, really?

682
00:26:02,774 --> 00:26:04,944
I drew on them. How do they look?

683
00:26:04,944 --> 00:26:06,174
The left one...

684
00:26:06,174 --> 00:26:07,614
- I think they look okay.
- The balance is important.

685
00:26:07,614 --> 00:26:09,544
- My eyebrows. Do they look okay?
- They look even.

686
00:26:09,544 --> 00:26:11,814
- Do they look even?
- They look okay to me.

687
00:26:12,454 --> 00:26:15,354
When we went home yesterday, my feelings were hurt.

688
00:26:15,354 --> 00:26:16,824
- Why?
- My left eyebrow looked weird,

689
00:26:16,824 --> 00:26:17,954
but you said it looked okay.

690
00:26:17,954 --> 00:26:20,124
- Are you trying to compete with me?
- I looked...

691
00:26:20,124 --> 00:26:21,124
- Oh, my goodness.
- It's not like that.

692
00:26:21,124 --> 00:26:22,924
From your left side,

693
00:26:22,924 --> 00:26:23,994
your left eyebrow looked fine.

694
00:26:23,994 --> 00:26:25,464
- I saw it in the bathroom...
- From your left side...

695
00:26:25,464 --> 00:26:26,534
and got surprised.

696
00:26:26,964 --> 00:26:29,304
- You kept it from me all day long.
- Oh, so you...

697
00:26:29,664 --> 00:26:31,404
Are you jealous of me?

698
00:26:32,204 --> 00:26:34,604
Are you competing with me in beauty or something?

699
00:26:34,844 --> 00:26:36,274
- Really?
- She clearly said...

700
00:26:36,274 --> 00:26:38,344
- my eyebrows looked fine.
- I mean, I was...

701
00:26:38,344 --> 00:26:40,344
I trusted her and showed my face to the cameras all day long.

702
00:26:40,344 --> 00:26:41,944
- You see, - But when I went home...

703
00:26:41,944 --> 00:26:43,984
there isn't a single jealous bone in my body.

704
00:26:43,984 --> 00:26:45,584
- When I went home, - Why would I...

705
00:26:45,584 --> 00:26:47,214
- I saw my eyebrows in the bathroom.
- Why would I be jealous...

706
00:26:47,384 --> 00:26:48,754
And my left eyebrow looked weird.

707
00:26:48,754 --> 00:26:50,584
Why did you tell me it looked okay?

708
00:26:50,584 --> 00:26:51,594
(Lost for words)

709
00:26:51,754 --> 00:26:53,324
- Because of you...
- I trusted you, Village Chief.

710
00:26:53,324 --> 00:26:54,864
So I thought my eyebrows...

711
00:26:54,864 --> 00:26:56,224
Why am I the village chief?

712
00:26:56,224 --> 00:26:58,334
If not you, who else is the village chief?

713
00:26:58,734 --> 00:27:00,164
Who's the head of this village?

714
00:27:00,164 --> 00:27:01,564
- The village chief...
- It's not like I know anyone here.

715
00:27:01,564 --> 00:27:03,964
- It should be you, Choon Ja.
- Who are you, then?

716
00:27:03,964 --> 00:27:05,974
How many times have I told you? I'm Yum Jung Ah.

717
00:27:06,234 --> 00:27:07,234
(Laughing)

718
00:27:07,234 --> 00:27:08,404
Oh, Yum Jung Ah?

719
00:27:08,604 --> 00:27:09,904
- You're just Yum Jung Ah?
- Yes.

720
00:27:09,904 --> 00:27:11,814
(She's very happy with her eyebrows today.)

721
00:27:12,144 --> 00:27:14,044
Her eyebrow episode is so funny.

722
00:27:14,444 --> 00:27:16,944
They look perfect now. They're just perfect.

723
00:27:17,644 --> 00:27:20,354
Did you sleep comfortably last night?

724
00:27:20,614 --> 00:27:22,324
I blinked, and it was morning.

725
00:27:22,324 --> 00:27:24,054
- That's great.
- Yes.

726
00:27:24,854 --> 00:27:26,324
He was knocked out the moment he lay down.

727
00:27:26,554 --> 00:27:27,654
- Right?
- Yes.

728
00:27:28,424 --> 00:27:29,694
Did you watch me sleep?

729
00:27:30,394 --> 00:27:31,394
(Chuckling)

730
00:27:32,094 --> 00:27:34,434
(He watched his role model sleep.)

731
00:27:34,434 --> 00:27:36,104
I wonder what we're going to do.

732
00:27:37,034 --> 00:27:38,634
I'm so curious.

733
00:27:38,774 --> 00:27:41,374
We're not working in Taean. We're heading to Seosan.

734
00:27:41,374 --> 00:27:42,944
- Are we heading to Seosan?
- Seosan?

735
00:27:42,944 --> 00:27:45,414
On our map, there are some drawings...

736
00:27:45,414 --> 00:27:47,674
in Seosan too, not just in Taean.

737
00:27:47,784 --> 00:27:49,284
- Seosan?
- It was either potato or garlic.

738
00:27:49,284 --> 00:27:50,284
I can't remember which one.

739
00:27:50,284 --> 00:27:51,714
Let's check what Seosan is famous for.

740
00:27:51,714 --> 00:27:53,214
- Seosan...
- So we're doing farm work.

741
00:27:53,654 --> 00:27:54,884
Guys, in Seosan,

742
00:27:55,224 --> 00:27:56,824
the Mount Palbong Potato Festival is held.

743
00:27:57,154 --> 00:27:58,524
- Potato?
- Potato?

744
00:27:58,654 --> 00:27:59,954
- So it's potato?
- It's potato.

745
00:27:59,954 --> 00:28:01,324
(Will they harvest potatoes today?)

746
00:28:02,194 --> 00:28:04,494
(As the car rolls along busily, )

747
00:28:04,494 --> 00:28:05,634
(rice paddies and fields stretch out before them.)

748
00:28:05,634 --> 00:28:06,864
It's right in front of us.

749
00:28:07,334 --> 00:28:08,734
Isn't that it?

750
00:28:08,734 --> 00:28:11,934
(Is that our destination?)

751
00:28:13,804 --> 00:28:15,474
Oh, my. This is huge.

752
00:28:15,474 --> 00:28:19,744
(The endless field is already packed with people.)

753
00:28:19,744 --> 00:28:22,884
There are some people who have already started working there.

754
00:28:22,884 --> 00:28:24,014
(The endless field is already packed with people.)

755
00:28:24,954 --> 00:28:26,954
(Current time: 8:30am)

756
00:28:28,224 --> 00:28:30,954
(Many people are working busily early in the morning.)

757
00:28:31,854 --> 00:28:34,394
(What is today's crop to harvest that's hidden beneath the soil?)

758
00:28:34,394 --> 00:28:35,394
Exactly.

759
00:28:35,394 --> 00:28:37,394
(Curious)

760
00:28:37,394 --> 00:28:38,564
Thank you for driving.

761
00:28:38,664 --> 00:28:40,394
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

762
00:28:40,634 --> 00:28:41,634
All right.

763
00:28:41,764 --> 00:28:42,904
What could it be?

764
00:28:43,264 --> 00:28:44,334
It's garlic.

765
00:28:44,934 --> 00:28:45,974
- Right? It's garlic.
- It's garlic.

766
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:47,074
It's obvious.

767
00:28:47,234 --> 00:28:49,344
Seeing how they're piled up, I guess the harvesting method is...

768
00:28:49,344 --> 00:28:50,874
- pretty similar to onions.
- Right.

769
00:28:52,014 --> 00:28:53,174
It's garlic, right?

770
00:28:54,844 --> 00:28:57,584
(That's correct. It's garlic.)

771
00:28:59,214 --> 00:29:00,414
Garlic grows well in this area.

772
00:29:01,054 --> 00:29:03,054
This land was reclaimed from the sea 40 years ago,

773
00:29:03,054 --> 00:29:05,524
and it has transformed into this fertile land.

774
00:29:07,294 --> 00:29:11,794
(All kinds of crops thrive in this soil.)

775
00:29:12,794 --> 00:29:13,864
(And the best crop among them is...)

776
00:29:13,864 --> 00:29:16,504
The garlic here is raised on the sea breeze,

777
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:17,664
making it high quality.

778
00:29:18,274 --> 00:29:20,974
It's rich in allicin,

779
00:29:21,344 --> 00:29:24,204
which makes the garlic good for your health.

780
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:26,774
(Garlic, the comfort ingredient for Koreans)

781
00:29:27,814 --> 00:29:31,044
(How do you harvest garlic?)

782
00:29:31,214 --> 00:29:32,384
- Hello.
- Hello.

783
00:29:32,384 --> 00:29:34,654
- It's nice to meet you all. Hello.
- Hello.

784
00:29:35,854 --> 00:29:37,424
I'll show you...

785
00:29:37,754 --> 00:29:39,854
- how to harvest garlic.
- Okay.

786
00:29:39,854 --> 00:29:41,464
You can see the garden forks over there.

787
00:29:41,824 --> 00:29:43,794
This is a garlic harvesting tool.

788
00:29:44,124 --> 00:29:46,294
The garlic is hidden under the soil right now.

789
00:29:46,664 --> 00:29:48,834
Hold the stem with one hand like this...

790
00:29:49,134 --> 00:29:50,734
and gently dig around it. Then, the garlic will pop out.

791
00:29:50,734 --> 00:29:51,734
(Dig around the garlic like this, and it's done.)

792
00:29:52,404 --> 00:29:54,744
(Dig in with the garden fork.)

793
00:29:54,744 --> 00:29:57,244
(Next, pull it up while scooping the soil.)

794
00:29:57,704 --> 00:29:59,274
(Digging in)

795
00:29:59,274 --> 00:30:00,744
(Pulling it up)

796
00:30:00,744 --> 00:30:02,684
(Digging in)

797
00:30:02,684 --> 00:30:04,244
(Pulling it up)

798
00:30:04,754 --> 00:30:07,154
You just have to loosen the soil. It's easy.

799
00:30:07,954 --> 00:30:09,654
But what if I stab the garlic while digging in?

800
00:30:09,954 --> 00:30:12,854
- Don't dig too close to the garlic.
- I see.

801
00:30:12,854 --> 00:30:13,954
Oh, so a bit further away from the garlic?

802
00:30:13,954 --> 00:30:16,064
Yes, dig a bit further away from the garlic like this.

803
00:30:17,724 --> 00:30:19,464
So we should slide it in diagonally.

804
00:30:21,404 --> 00:30:24,134
(That way, you won't damage the garlic.)

805
00:30:24,304 --> 00:30:25,534
- Try it for now.
- Okay.

806
00:30:25,534 --> 00:30:26,574
- Got it.
- Okay.

807
00:30:27,374 --> 00:30:29,474
- You make it look so easy.
- Yes.

808
00:30:29,774 --> 00:30:31,744
- Try it.
- Slide it in like this...

809
00:30:31,974 --> 00:30:33,244
- It pops out, right?
- Yes, it pops out.

810
00:30:33,614 --> 00:30:35,244
- Good.
- Oh, I get it.

811
00:30:35,314 --> 00:30:39,114
After you finish digging up all the garlic here...

812
00:30:39,184 --> 00:30:40,214
Yes.

813
00:30:40,554 --> 00:30:42,384
This part is the stem.

814
00:30:43,484 --> 00:30:46,324
- Cut off the stem like this.
- Yes.

815
00:30:47,294 --> 00:30:48,624
Cut the stem off...

816
00:30:48,624 --> 00:30:49,894
(Once you get all the garlic bulbs piled up like this...)

817
00:30:50,094 --> 00:30:51,764
And put them all in the net.

818
00:30:51,964 --> 00:30:53,364
- Right away?
- Put them in the net... Yes.

819
00:30:53,364 --> 00:30:54,394
Got it.

820
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:55,564
Okay.

821
00:30:55,564 --> 00:30:58,034
(You have to pack the net with garlic bulbs like this.)

822
00:30:58,304 --> 00:31:00,604
Let's begin. We'll move forward.

823
00:31:01,074 --> 00:31:02,304
- Let's begin.
- Start digging them up.

824
00:31:03,074 --> 00:31:06,114
Should I put it aside after pulling it out?

825
00:31:06,214 --> 00:31:07,644
- Or should I carry it?
- Just put it on the ground.

826
00:31:07,644 --> 00:31:09,284
- Okay.
- And we'll cut them all at once.

827
00:31:09,284 --> 00:31:10,344
(Let's dig them up first and then cut the stems off at once.)

828
00:31:11,514 --> 00:31:13,154
Yes, that's good.

829
00:31:13,784 --> 00:31:14,784
Good.

830
00:31:16,054 --> 00:31:17,684
Nice.

831
00:31:17,684 --> 00:31:20,794
(They all focus on digging up the garlic for now.)

832
00:31:24,764 --> 00:31:26,734
The garlic looks so fresh and plump.

833
00:31:28,064 --> 00:31:31,234
In my opinion, the key is to harvest the garlic...

834
00:31:31,234 --> 00:31:32,974
without damaging it.

835
00:31:33,274 --> 00:31:34,334
- Right.
- I agree.

836
00:31:36,674 --> 00:31:38,314
Oh, my. This is fun.

837
00:31:39,814 --> 00:31:40,844
Yes, indeed.

838
00:31:42,184 --> 00:31:43,244
It's the best.

839
00:31:43,944 --> 00:31:46,114
It's so cool how they grow underground like this.

840
00:31:46,114 --> 00:31:48,084
(Pulling them up is satisfying.)

841
00:31:48,754 --> 00:31:49,824
Look. There are two bulbs under a single stem.

842
00:31:51,054 --> 00:31:53,154
- You got twins.
- Two bulbs?

843
00:31:53,154 --> 00:31:54,394
(The four siblings and Jung Seok are locked in on the garlic harvest.)

844
00:31:54,394 --> 00:31:55,464
This only takes a second.

845
00:31:57,464 --> 00:31:58,894
How much do we get per kilogram?

846
00:31:59,594 --> 00:32:02,804
One full net weighs about 10kg.

847
00:32:03,564 --> 00:32:05,834
We'll pay you 15 dollars per net.

848
00:32:05,834 --> 00:32:07,634
- We get 15 dollars per net?
- Did she say 10kg?

849
00:32:08,604 --> 00:32:09,674
We're done for.

850
00:32:10,774 --> 00:32:11,874
That means it's 1.50 dollars per kilogram.

851
00:32:12,774 --> 00:32:14,244
That's so cheap.

852
00:32:15,544 --> 00:32:17,414
How much money do you have left?

853
00:32:17,514 --> 00:32:20,484
- Why? Why do you ask?
- We have no money left.

854
00:32:20,484 --> 00:32:23,684
Why do you want to know how much we have left?

855
00:32:24,184 --> 00:32:26,254
Exactly. That's just strange.

856
00:32:26,254 --> 00:32:27,454
Why does it matter?

857
00:32:28,224 --> 00:32:30,194
We have no money.

858
00:32:31,534 --> 00:32:32,534
We have no money left.

859
00:32:32,534 --> 00:32:36,634
(In that case, you should work hard, right?)

860
00:32:37,104 --> 00:32:38,174
This one is big.

861
00:32:38,404 --> 00:32:40,804
Oh, boy. My dear Jung Ja is...

862
00:32:40,804 --> 00:32:42,344
working with us for 2 rounds, not just 1.

863
00:32:42,344 --> 00:32:45,444
(How did I end up working again?)

864
00:32:47,044 --> 00:32:48,444
Jung Seok, if you...

865
00:32:48,944 --> 00:32:51,344
take some garlic home, will Gummy be happy?

866
00:32:51,714 --> 00:32:54,554
- That's okay.
- Tell her you harvested them.

867
00:32:54,554 --> 00:32:56,124
- You should take some home.
- You should.

868
00:32:56,124 --> 00:32:57,284
You're really giving me some garlic?

869
00:32:57,284 --> 00:32:59,754
- Sure.
- It'd be nice to cook something...

870
00:32:59,754 --> 00:33:02,124
with the garlic that you harvested by yourself.

871
00:33:02,724 --> 00:33:04,264
You see...

872
00:33:04,794 --> 00:33:08,334
Thinking about how hard you guys should work...

873
00:33:08,334 --> 00:33:09,504
to make money even after I leave...

874
00:33:09,604 --> 00:33:12,204
breaks my heart. I'd feel too bad taking anything home.

875
00:33:12,204 --> 00:33:13,204
That's okay. You should take some home.

876
00:33:13,304 --> 00:33:16,174
Our work will be done after this.

877
00:33:16,174 --> 00:33:17,344
- It'll be over.
- We'll only have fun.

878
00:33:17,344 --> 00:33:18,814
- Right.
- Are you sure?

879
00:33:19,514 --> 00:33:21,414
- I asked if you were sure.
- I'm not sure about it.

880
00:33:21,414 --> 00:33:23,344
Village Chief, are you sure?

881
00:33:23,984 --> 00:33:26,154
- Why do you keep calling me that?
- "Village Chief..."

882
00:33:27,054 --> 00:33:29,784
How many times have I told you she's not the village chief?

883
00:33:30,854 --> 00:33:33,654
With the way things are going, who's the village chief?

884
00:33:34,524 --> 00:33:36,894
(Laughing)

885
00:33:37,594 --> 00:33:38,894
Sun Young, this one is huge.

886
00:33:39,364 --> 00:33:40,734
This one has a baby.

887
00:33:40,734 --> 00:33:42,604
Good job, my dear Yoon Seo.

888
00:33:43,504 --> 00:33:45,534
- You don't sound like you mean it.
- You did a great job.

889
00:33:45,534 --> 00:33:49,104
- Say it like you mean it.
- I like everything about you.

890
00:33:49,104 --> 00:33:50,474
I really like you.

891
00:33:51,274 --> 00:33:53,244
- That sounds soulless.
- I mean it.

892
00:33:53,244 --> 00:33:54,544
I'm nothing without my soul.

893
00:33:55,084 --> 00:33:56,744
- It's "soul" in English.
- Okay.

894
00:33:56,744 --> 00:33:57,844
(Nobody is whole without their soul.)

895
00:33:58,814 --> 00:34:00,384
(Meanwhile, Captain Yum is full of garlic soul.)

896
00:34:00,384 --> 00:34:01,454
Look at this garlic.

897
00:34:01,454 --> 00:34:02,454
(Meanwhile, Captain Yum is full of garlic soul.)

898
00:34:03,454 --> 00:34:05,354
(Amazed)

899
00:34:06,894 --> 00:34:08,664
(She dusts the dirt off carefully.)

900
00:34:09,124 --> 00:34:14,234
(She quietly stacks up the garlic she harvested.)

901
00:34:14,904 --> 00:34:17,964
(30 minutes have passed.)

902
00:34:19,104 --> 00:34:21,304
Am I a master or what? I'm so good at this.

903
00:34:21,304 --> 00:34:22,744
(I'm so good at this.)

904
00:34:23,544 --> 00:34:25,444
I got the hang of it. Good.

905
00:34:26,214 --> 00:34:27,644
I think I'm doing great.

906
00:34:28,074 --> 00:34:29,684
- Exactly.
- What?

907
00:34:29,684 --> 00:34:31,614
- Exactly.
- We're all thinking the same thing.

908
00:34:31,614 --> 00:34:34,414
- "Why am I so good at this?"
- I was thinking that too.

909
00:34:34,824 --> 00:34:35,824
I can do it in one second.

910
00:34:36,984 --> 00:34:39,294
I'm doing it alone, and look how fast I'm doing it.

911
00:34:39,694 --> 00:34:41,924
- Ready.
- Ready, go.

912
00:34:41,924 --> 00:34:43,164
(They suddenly start competing.)

913
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:44,364
- One.
- Three.

914
00:34:45,264 --> 00:34:46,434
Four.

915
00:34:46,434 --> 00:34:48,204
(Since we're doing this anyway, we might as well have fun with it.)

916
00:34:48,204 --> 00:34:49,204
Ten.

917
00:34:49,734 --> 00:34:50,804
Eleven.

918
00:34:50,804 --> 00:34:51,934
(She dusts off the dirt even during the competition.)

919
00:34:52,634 --> 00:34:55,344
- Thirteen, fourteen...
- Yoon Seo is doing really great.

920
00:34:55,344 --> 00:34:56,744
Maybe Yoon Seo is not doing it properly.

921
00:34:57,374 --> 00:34:58,844
Is it really possible to do it that fast?

922
00:34:59,174 --> 00:35:00,774
- That's it. It's over.
- Okay.

923
00:35:01,444 --> 00:35:03,344
- Yoon Seo dug up seventeen.
- Seventeen?

924
00:35:03,344 --> 00:35:04,954
I got six.

925
00:35:05,284 --> 00:35:08,154
- You're in the bottom place.
- I thought I was good at this.

926
00:35:08,484 --> 00:35:09,754
- Sun Young, - Why?

927
00:35:09,754 --> 00:35:10,984
you don't want to do this, do you?

928
00:35:10,984 --> 00:35:12,994
(While they laugh and work, the garlic pile grows quickly.)

929
00:35:13,524 --> 00:35:14,964
Oh, gosh. There's a bee here.

930
00:35:15,664 --> 00:35:16,664
- A bee came to you?
- Yes.

931
00:35:17,294 --> 00:35:18,834
Yoon Seo must be a flower.

932
00:35:20,994 --> 00:35:23,104
(The joke really got him.)

933
00:35:23,804 --> 00:35:25,904
(She lost her drive.)

934
00:35:26,204 --> 00:35:27,404
You're not a boat captain...

935
00:35:27,804 --> 00:35:29,244
- I'm the village chief.
- You're the village chief?

936
00:35:29,244 --> 00:35:31,044
- You're the village chief?
- Oh, he's the village chief.

937
00:35:31,044 --> 00:35:32,674
- I'm the village chief.
- I didn't know that.

938
00:35:32,674 --> 00:35:35,014
I mistook Choon Ja for the one.

939
00:35:35,514 --> 00:35:38,384
Look how fast she flipped the switch.

940
00:35:38,384 --> 00:35:40,314
Hearts are about to shoot out of my eyes.

941
00:35:40,314 --> 00:35:41,314
(1 hour into the garlic harvest)

942
00:35:42,554 --> 00:35:45,024
(They pull out the garlic.)

943
00:35:45,024 --> 00:35:47,624
(And they repeat it.)

944
00:35:48,664 --> 00:35:51,324
(And they dust the dirt off.)

945
00:35:51,694 --> 00:35:52,794
I'm exhausted.

946
00:35:54,194 --> 00:35:57,234
- We have to chop the stems too.
- Exactly.

947
00:35:58,164 --> 00:35:59,434
I've been experiencing many things.

948
00:36:00,674 --> 00:36:03,304
- When do we ever get to do this?
- Exactly.

949
00:36:03,844 --> 00:36:06,744
- We should always be grateful.
- That motivates you.

950
00:36:07,814 --> 00:36:10,084
(A thought crosses her mind.)

951
00:36:10,084 --> 00:36:11,384
I don't know why,

952
00:36:11,754 --> 00:36:14,814
but I feel like I've been sitting here since yesterday.

953
00:36:15,884 --> 00:36:17,824
- Sitting on this stool.
- Oh, that's right.

954
00:36:18,554 --> 00:36:21,994
(Am I living in yesterday or today?)

955
00:36:22,564 --> 00:36:23,724
You said the same thing yesterday. You know that, right?

956
00:36:24,564 --> 00:36:26,964
- "When do we ever get to do this?"
- Right.

957
00:36:27,234 --> 00:36:30,434
We worked with a hoe yesterday. Today, we're digging again.

958
00:36:30,734 --> 00:36:33,934
What do you call this part? It hurts so much right here.

959
00:36:34,034 --> 00:36:35,674
- We dug with a hoe yesterday.
- Right.

960
00:36:35,674 --> 00:36:37,104
- We're using our hands so much.
- And today,

961
00:36:37,104 --> 00:36:38,574
- we're using the same muscle.
- It hurts right here, right?

962
00:36:38,574 --> 00:36:41,174
What's the anatomic term for this part?

963
00:36:41,174 --> 00:36:42,184
Handgrip.

964
00:36:42,184 --> 00:36:43,514
- Handgrip?
- Is it called handgrip?

965
00:36:43,514 --> 00:36:44,814
Isn't it handgrip?

966
00:36:44,914 --> 00:36:46,554
(Let's just forget it.)

967
00:36:47,014 --> 00:36:50,724
Oh, dear. I wish I could have a cup of coffee. Right?

968
00:36:50,724 --> 00:36:52,724
- Yes, of course.
- You don't even have to say it.

969
00:36:52,724 --> 00:36:55,524
- No need to say it.
- That's a luxury for us right now.

970
00:36:56,564 --> 00:36:58,124
(If that's the case...)

971
00:36:58,434 --> 00:37:00,594
How about we play a game again?

972
00:37:01,494 --> 00:37:03,604
Don't you guys want...

973
00:37:03,604 --> 00:37:05,634
a cup of nice, cold iced Americano?

974
00:37:05,634 --> 00:37:08,174
- Jung Ah.
- Let's play a game...

975
00:37:08,174 --> 00:37:09,904
- with coffee on the line.
- Do you want to play a game?

976
00:37:09,904 --> 00:37:11,244
The winning team gets drinks.

977
00:37:11,444 --> 00:37:12,974
Say something.

978
00:37:13,144 --> 00:37:15,384
You invited me here and made me work twice.

979
00:37:15,484 --> 00:37:18,044
- How about a garlic digging match?
- That's a good idea.

980
00:37:18,354 --> 00:37:20,884
- One of you against one of us.
- Okay.

981
00:37:21,254 --> 00:37:23,654
- If you dig up more garlic bulbs...
- In one minute.

982
00:37:23,654 --> 00:37:24,684
in one minute, you win.

983
00:37:24,994 --> 00:37:27,994
- Oh, that's a great idea.
- I'm confident.

984
00:37:29,064 --> 00:37:30,164
What if you lose?

985
00:37:30,724 --> 00:37:32,964
I haven't even considered that.

986
00:37:33,164 --> 00:37:34,264
If you lose, you buy the staff coffee.

987
00:37:34,694 --> 00:37:37,264
- Okay. We'll buy you coffee.
- But we don't have that much money.

988
00:37:37,734 --> 00:37:39,834
I have a credit card.

989
00:37:40,174 --> 00:37:42,474
- Right. She'll treat you.
- I'll treat you.

990
00:37:42,474 --> 00:37:44,444
- Right. She'll buy you coffee.
- Okay.

991
00:37:45,174 --> 00:37:46,214
Deal?

992
00:37:46,214 --> 00:37:47,344
(Deal)

993
00:37:47,844 --> 00:37:49,614
Who represents the production staff? Come forward.

994
00:37:49,614 --> 00:37:50,644
- Come forward.
- Come forward.

995
00:37:50,644 --> 00:37:52,314
- Yoon Seo will represent the cast.
- Let's do this!

996
00:37:53,154 --> 00:37:54,154
Bring it on.

997
00:37:55,224 --> 00:37:56,384
What's your nickname?

998
00:37:56,884 --> 00:37:58,854
- Nickname...
- What's your nickname?

999
00:37:58,994 --> 00:37:59,994
Special Forces.

1000
00:38:00,094 --> 00:38:02,894
- "Special Forces?" That's not fair.
- But...

1001
00:38:02,964 --> 00:38:04,024
- Special Forces?
- Special Forces?

1002
00:38:04,024 --> 00:38:05,634
Hold on. A former Special Forces agent against me?

1003
00:38:06,694 --> 00:38:08,094
Isn't that a really scary place?

1004
00:38:08,464 --> 00:38:10,104
Actually, I have another nickname.

1005
00:38:10,364 --> 00:38:11,804
It's "Son of Namhae."

1006
00:38:11,804 --> 00:38:13,704
- Son of Namhae against...
- Namhae is also famous for garlic.

1007
00:38:13,704 --> 00:38:17,274
He served in the Special Forces and has farming experience.

1008
00:38:17,274 --> 00:38:18,744
- Son of Namhae.
- You're telling me...

1009
00:38:19,274 --> 00:38:20,774
Namhae? Have you ever harvested garlic?

1010
00:38:22,184 --> 00:38:24,044
(Of course)

1011
00:38:24,814 --> 00:38:26,954
- You have a lot of experience, yes?
- Yes.

1012
00:38:27,184 --> 00:38:28,684
He's the one who found this field.

1013
00:38:28,984 --> 00:38:31,084
(So what?)

