01:26:58,231 --> 01:26:59,671
- You Soon is coming up right now.
- You Soon.

2287
01:26:59,731 --> 01:27:01,671
You Soon shocked me.

2288
01:27:01,901 --> 01:27:03,071
He looks so good.

2289
01:27:03,241 --> 01:27:05,141
- Gosh.
- He's coming.

2290
01:27:06,611 --> 01:27:10,011
(The last model strides in.)

2291
01:27:10,181 --> 01:27:11,181
Come on.

2292
01:27:11,311 --> 01:27:15,281
- Come on.
- Come on.

2293
01:27:18,551 --> 01:27:19,951
- Come on.
- Come on.

2294
01:27:19,951 --> 01:27:23,421
(The last model, You Soon, the tough guy)

2295
01:27:23,421 --> 01:27:24,491
It's crazy.

2296
01:27:24,931 --> 01:27:27,391
(Throwing on)

2297
01:27:27,931 --> 01:27:31,701
(Unleashing his wild energy)

2298
01:27:31,801 --> 01:27:33,301
Why is everyone so good at this?

2299
01:27:33,301 --> 01:27:35,401
- "I'm James Dean."
- Gosh.

2300
01:27:35,801 --> 01:27:37,871
- Are you James Dean?
- Why is he crushing it?

2301
01:27:38,641 --> 01:27:41,271
(Do you know You James?)

2302
01:27:42,041 --> 01:27:44,311
(The grand return...)

2303
01:27:44,311 --> 01:27:47,681
(of the 1970s rebellious bad boy)

2304
01:27:48,021 --> 01:27:50,321
(Denim-on-denim and a red scarf)

2305
01:27:50,321 --> 01:27:53,021
(The epitome of a Western tough guy)

2306
01:27:55,921 --> 01:27:58,061
(The man of the American West...)

2307
01:27:58,061 --> 01:27:59,291
(is here to conquer the Korean West.)

2308
01:27:59,291 --> 01:28:00,291
(Clacking)

2309
01:28:04,461 --> 01:28:05,501
Please go on.

2310
01:28:05,501 --> 01:28:08,501
(Laughing)

2311
01:28:08,841 --> 01:28:12,671
(Anyway, he's You James Dean.)

2312
01:28:12,871 --> 01:28:16,511
(He has an irresistible charm.)

2313
01:28:17,711 --> 01:28:20,511
(But don't fall for him.)

2314
01:28:20,751 --> 01:28:22,551
- Why is he crushing it?
- Are you James Dean?

2315
01:28:22,551 --> 01:28:24,581
Gosh. I lost. I need to redo this.

2316
01:28:24,581 --> 01:28:25,851
I need to come back.

2317
01:28:26,091 --> 01:28:27,951
- I'll make the entrance again.
- Where are you going?

2318
01:28:28,561 --> 01:28:31,431
(Turning one more time)

2319
01:28:31,661 --> 01:28:35,061
(Putting on a good show)

2320
01:28:36,301 --> 01:28:37,301
(Celebrating)

2321
01:28:37,301 --> 01:28:39,601
- He's crazy.
- Good job.

2322
01:28:39,731 --> 01:28:42,101
- Why is he so good?
- He's awesome.

2323
01:28:42,401 --> 01:28:46,471
(He's not done yet.)

2324
01:28:46,911 --> 01:28:48,941
- He's my nephew.
- Okay.

2325
01:28:48,941 --> 01:28:50,941
You look amazing, You Soon.

2326
01:28:51,451 --> 01:28:52,911
He was influenced by his aunt...

2327
01:28:52,911 --> 01:28:54,251
- after staying with her.
- He speaks good Korean.

2328
01:28:54,481 --> 01:28:58,091
(He was influenced, all right.)

2329
01:28:58,091 --> 01:28:59,921
(He was heavily influenced by her.)

2330
01:29:00,251 --> 01:29:01,251
(Madness and fear)

2331
01:29:01,251 --> 01:29:02,521
Jung Ah, what do we do?

2332
01:29:02,521 --> 01:29:04,091
We can't pull that off because we're so pretty.

2333
01:29:04,091 --> 01:29:06,131
I'm so shocked and touched.

2334
01:29:06,531 --> 01:29:07,931
- Hold my hand.
- What do I do?

2335
01:29:07,931 --> 01:29:09,131
I'm no match for them.

2336
01:29:09,301 --> 01:29:10,961
Hold on. You Seok.

2337
01:29:10,961 --> 01:29:12,101
We're a couple.

2338
01:29:12,101 --> 01:29:13,431
(The two went on...)

2339
01:29:13,431 --> 01:29:17,671
(to let it all out.)

2340
01:29:17,671 --> 01:29:19,571
Okay. Good.

2341
01:29:19,571 --> 01:29:21,441
(Admiring them)

2342
01:29:21,681 --> 01:29:24,411
- Let's take a family photo.
- How could you, You Seok?

2343
01:29:24,411 --> 01:29:27,781
Gosh. I'm back to myself. I was possessed by someone else.

2344
01:29:28,651 --> 01:29:30,551
Jung Ah, you look so pretty, though.

2345
01:29:31,021 --> 01:29:32,521
- You're really pretty.
- Especially the tights.

2346
01:29:32,521 --> 01:29:33,551
(Thanks for the compliments.)

2347
01:29:33,551 --> 01:29:35,021
- You're in your element.
- It's...

2348
01:29:36,091 --> 01:29:39,061
Shouldn't we go clubbing like this?

2349
01:29:39,291 --> 01:29:41,931
- I saw you going crazy.
- Hello. We'll take a family photo.

2350
01:29:41,931 --> 01:29:43,531
(It's really time to take a family photo.)

2351
01:29:44,561 --> 01:29:47,731
(First, they will take solo shots to commemorate the moment.)

2352
01:29:52,141 --> 01:29:53,211
You're crushing it, Jung Ah.

2353
01:29:54,741 --> 01:29:57,841
(Yoon Seo is crushing it too.)

2354
01:29:58,151 --> 01:29:59,181
It's S.O.S.

2355
01:30:01,181 --> 01:30:02,881
- Did you say S.O.S?
- Yes, S.O.S.

2356
01:30:03,021 --> 01:30:05,421
(Glaring)

2357
01:30:05,651 --> 01:30:07,391
Please take photos of me.

2358
01:30:07,391 --> 01:30:08,661
(Aunt Jennica gets solo shots too.)

2359
01:30:09,661 --> 01:30:11,121
(Stumbling)

2360
01:30:11,891 --> 01:30:13,161
Please give me a second. It was nothing.

2361
01:30:13,161 --> 01:30:14,331
(She's still not used to the killer heels.)

2362
01:30:15,001 --> 01:30:18,501
(You James Dean is looking cool too.)

2363
01:30:19,401 --> 01:30:21,031
(He even takes it to the floor.)

2364
01:30:21,031 --> 01:30:23,401
Gosh. My goodness.

2365
01:30:23,941 --> 01:30:26,241
(After taking the solo shots, )

2366
01:30:26,241 --> 01:30:27,241
It's insane.

2367
01:30:27,541 --> 01:30:31,681
(it's time for a family photo.)

2368
01:30:34,151 --> 01:30:36,251
(Cracking up)

2369
01:30:36,651 --> 01:30:39,951
(The family looks a bit eccentric.)

2370
01:30:40,551 --> 01:30:45,661
(But they will remember today's happy and fun moments...)

2371
01:30:48,201 --> 01:30:50,031
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2372
01:30:50,031 --> 01:30:52,231
(with their first family photo.)

2373
01:30:52,571 --> 01:30:54,871
- Thank you.
- Good job.

2374
01:30:54,871 --> 01:30:55,901
(The siblings come home after shopping for groceries.)

2375
01:30:56,941 --> 01:30:58,911
- Let's rest for a bit, Jung Ah.
- Let's get some rest.

2376
01:31:00,171 --> 01:31:01,781
Gosh. What a lovely day.

2377
01:31:01,981 --> 01:31:04,681
(Jennica lounges in the afternoon sun.)

2378
01:31:05,181 --> 01:31:08,051
(The sun above their heads sinks toward the ground.)

2379
01:31:08,521 --> 01:31:11,281
(And evening has come, painting the fields in golden hues.)

2380
01:31:12,291 --> 01:31:14,891
Can someone help me carry it?

2381
01:31:14,891 --> 01:31:15,991
It's too heavy for me.

2382
01:31:16,321 --> 01:31:18,931
(You Seok goes to the kitchen to help Jung Ah.)

2383
01:31:19,291 --> 01:31:21,161
- The pig's feet?
- Yes.

2384
01:31:21,701 --> 01:31:24,761
(Pig's feet!)

2385
01:31:25,571 --> 01:31:27,531
- Where should I put them?
- By the faucet.

2386
01:31:28,101 --> 01:31:29,141
I need to wash them.

2387
01:31:29,771 --> 01:31:33,041
(What is their dinner menu made with this many pig's feet?)

2388
01:31:33,271 --> 01:31:34,441
We'll make jokbal.

2389
01:31:34,541 --> 01:31:37,941
We'll also make garlic sauce with the garlic we received today.

2390
01:31:38,211 --> 01:31:40,751
And we'll make the bibim makguksu, the spicy buckwheat noodles.

2391
01:31:41,181 --> 01:31:43,921
And stir-fried garlic scapes with dried shrimp. That's all.

2392
01:31:45,021 --> 01:31:48,191
(The four siblings harvested...)

2393
01:31:49,321 --> 01:31:51,761
(Seosan's garlic, raised in an open field under the sun.)

2394
01:31:53,231 --> 01:31:55,661
(The garlic will add a pungent aroma to the table.)

2395
01:31:56,661 --> 01:31:57,731
Hello.

2396
01:31:58,901 --> 01:32:01,501
I'm going to make the seasoned dried radish.

2397
01:32:01,941 --> 01:32:03,371
Today, I'm the chef of the seasoned dried radish.

2398
01:32:03,371 --> 01:32:05,171
(You Seok's seasoned dried radish to enjoy with jokbal)

2399
01:32:05,471 --> 01:32:07,871
(The four siblings get to work to make dinner.)

2400
01:32:08,781 --> 01:32:11,651
(The Californian Wasp is the first one to get moving.)

2401
01:32:12,911 --> 01:32:14,311
Gosh. This garlic is amazing.

2402
01:32:15,351 --> 01:32:17,251
(She admires the garlic they harvested.)

2403
01:32:17,581 --> 01:32:18,651
This much?

2404
01:32:18,651 --> 01:32:19,651
(Checking the amount by grabbing a handful)

2405
01:32:20,121 --> 01:32:21,791
- You'll need more.
- More?

2406
01:32:21,791 --> 01:32:23,361
- Yes, it's because...
- Okay.

2407
01:32:23,461 --> 01:32:26,791
(Wasp Sun Young does not wait. She goes back before hearing why.)

2408
01:32:27,231 --> 01:32:30,561
I need to add some garlic when boiling the pig's feet.

2409
01:32:31,331 --> 01:32:33,071
(Adding twice as much)

2410
01:32:33,431 --> 01:32:35,041
Will twice as much be enough, Jung Ah?

2411
01:32:35,641 --> 01:32:36,641
Yes.

2412
01:32:36,641 --> 01:32:37,671
(Final approval)

2413
01:32:38,241 --> 01:32:39,811
(The Californian Wasp starts prepping the garlic...)

2414
01:32:39,811 --> 01:32:41,341
(after getting the approval.)

2415
01:32:42,581 --> 01:32:43,881
I need to sit on the floor.

2416
01:32:44,911 --> 01:32:47,251
(She adjusts herself to peel the garlic.)

2417
01:32:48,051 --> 01:32:49,881
This garlic is very fresh.

2418
01:32:50,421 --> 01:32:52,091
- Is it crazy?
- It's great.

2419
01:32:52,091 --> 01:32:54,351
(It's great.)

2420
01:32:55,161 --> 01:32:58,091
(Looking at the fresh garlic reminds her of...)

2421
01:32:58,861 --> 01:33:00,761
Back in California,

2422
01:33:00,761 --> 01:33:02,331
I couldn't find garlic...

2423
01:33:02,331 --> 01:33:04,961
that was in good quality like this.

2424
01:33:04,961 --> 01:33:06,971
(her one-month stay in California.)

2425
01:33:07,331 --> 01:33:09,601
It's really hard to run into garlic that's as fine as this.

2426
01:33:10,041 --> 01:33:12,271
What sets Korean garlic apart... What was it?

2427
01:33:12,271 --> 01:33:13,941
(She asks because she doesn't know.)

2428
01:33:14,941 --> 01:33:16,481
(Laughing)

2429
01:33:16,641 --> 01:33:17,741
My hands...

2430
01:33:18,381 --> 01:33:20,951
will smell like garlic.

2431
01:33:21,551 --> 01:33:23,581
Will you rinse the pig's feet, Yoon Seo?

2432
01:33:24,181 --> 01:33:26,091
- Okay.
- Can you touch them?

2433
01:33:26,191 --> 01:33:27,191
Yes.

2434
01:33:27,191 --> 01:33:30,121
Rinse them in case there's any bone dust.

2435
01:33:31,891 --> 01:33:33,191
(Jennica is now on the wooden platform...)

2436
01:33:33,191 --> 01:33:34,461
(to peel the garlic.)

2437
01:33:35,531 --> 01:33:38,571
I'm trying to peel the garlic when I'm from California.

2438
01:33:39,101 --> 01:33:40,631
I'm not used to this.

2439
01:33:41,701 --> 01:33:43,741
Do they not eat garlic in California?

2440
01:33:44,371 --> 01:33:46,211
- They eat it.
- Do they not have it?

2441
01:33:46,211 --> 01:33:48,711
I've never peeled the garlic before.

2442
01:33:50,041 --> 01:33:52,611
I'll keep peeling the garlic.

2443
01:33:53,511 --> 01:33:54,511
I'll stay seated.

2444
01:33:54,511 --> 01:33:55,551
(There is quite a lot of peeled garlic now.)

2445
01:33:56,251 --> 01:33:57,551
Please give me the garlic.

2446
01:33:57,551 --> 01:34:00,191
(Jung Ah gets ready to make the garlic sauce.)

2447
01:34:00,751 --> 01:34:01,761
Yes.

2448
01:34:03,191 --> 01:34:04,261
That will be enough.

2449
01:34:04,361 --> 01:34:05,361
- Is it enough?
- Yes.

2450
01:34:05,361 --> 01:34:06,431
(Is she finally finished peeling garlic?)

2451
01:34:06,731 --> 01:34:08,191
(This is enough.)

2452
01:34:08,191 --> 01:34:09,501
Peel the rest...

2453
01:34:09,501 --> 01:34:10,531
(Peel the garlic to use when boiling the pig's feet.)

2454
01:34:10,531 --> 01:34:11,561
- to put in the water.
- Okay.

2455
01:34:12,331 --> 01:34:14,001
Please wash it to remove the skin completely.

2456
01:34:14,701 --> 01:34:17,471
Next time, let's not harvest garlic.

2457
01:34:19,211 --> 01:34:20,411
Let's just buy it.

2458
01:34:20,411 --> 01:34:23,541
(Let's buy garlic from a store.)

2459
01:34:24,011 --> 01:34:26,911
(Jennica asks or politely threatens the production staff.)

2460
01:34:27,311 --> 01:34:29,681
(Now, she's making the sauce.)

2461
01:34:30,221 --> 01:34:33,151
(Making garlic sauce, Step 1: Rinse the peeled garlic.)

2462
01:34:33,921 --> 01:34:36,461
(Making garlic sauce, Step 1: Mince the garlic.)

2463
01:34:36,861 --> 01:34:38,791
(Add the garlic to the chopper.)

2464
01:34:39,631 --> 01:34:42,601
(Mincing it with both hands)

2465
01:34:43,631 --> 01:34:44,901
(Let me see.)

2466
01:34:45,931 --> 01:34:46,971
What?

2467
01:34:48,271 --> 01:34:50,971
(It didn't get minced.)

2468
01:34:51,811 --> 01:34:53,811
It'll take forever to mince it. It won't work.

2469
01:34:55,011 --> 01:34:56,041
I'll try it.

2470
01:34:56,041 --> 01:34:57,041
(Let me try it.)

2471
01:34:57,041 --> 01:35:00,381
I tried it. You chop it by pushing it.

2472
01:35:03,481 --> 01:35:04,551
(Mincing it as if it's propelled by a motor)

2473
01:35:04,781 --> 01:35:07,291
(Bending over)

2474
01:35:07,691 --> 01:35:09,561
(He must be desperate to mince the garlic.)

2475
01:35:10,421 --> 01:35:12,361
- It's not moving inside.
- No. It doesn't work.

2476
01:35:12,791 --> 01:35:14,431
(It's still whole.)

2477
01:35:14,731 --> 01:35:15,761
Should I pound it?

2478
01:35:16,661 --> 01:35:17,701
That's right.

2479
01:35:18,701 --> 01:35:21,001
I'll pound it. It'll be done in no time.

2480
01:35:22,501 --> 01:35:23,971
- I need to crush it, right?
- Yes.

2481
01:35:23,971 --> 01:35:26,071
(He starts to pound it in a mortar, their new weapon.)

2482
01:35:26,971 --> 01:35:28,011
(The cameraman approaches.)

2483
01:35:28,011 --> 01:35:29,111
I...

2484
01:35:29,741 --> 01:35:30,811
I...

2485
01:35:31,081 --> 01:35:32,811
I've minced garlic many times.

2486
01:35:33,211 --> 01:35:35,111
- Really?
- At my grandma's place,

2487
01:35:35,111 --> 01:35:36,481
(He got his garlic-mincing skills at his grandma's place.)

2488
01:35:36,851 --> 01:35:40,421
I pounded garlic like this or used a garlic press.

2489
01:35:40,821 --> 01:35:42,761
Right. My mom used to use it all the time too.

2490
01:35:44,161 --> 01:35:47,531
I minced garlic many times to help my grandma.

2491
01:35:47,531 --> 01:35:48,631
(The garlic-mincing prodigy is lost in memories.)

2492
01:35:48,731 --> 01:35:50,661
Yes. This is how it's done.

2493
01:35:50,661 --> 01:35:52,071
(You Seok, lost in his memories, minces garlic for a long time.)

2494
01:35:53,071 --> 01:35:54,101
Is it done?

2495
01:35:54,901 --> 01:35:57,301
- Do you want it minced more finely?
- No.

2496
01:35:58,341 --> 01:36:00,011
(Thanks to You Seok, the garlic-mincing prodigy, )

2497
01:36:00,011 --> 01:36:01,641
(the garlic is finely minced.)

2498
01:36:02,111 --> 01:36:03,181
(Sugar)

2499
01:36:04,241 --> 01:36:05,311
(Vinegar)

2500
01:36:06,781 --> 01:36:07,781
(Oligosaccharide)

2501
01:36:08,981 --> 01:36:09,981
(Tuna fish sauce)

2502
01:36:11,481 --> 01:36:12,551
(Sesame oil)

2503
01:36:13,951 --> 01:36:16,821
(Mix the various ingredients well.)

2504
01:36:17,521 --> 01:36:18,931
(Cover it and let it sit for a while.)

2505
01:36:19,291 --> 01:36:21,691
(The garlic sauce is done.)

2506
01:36:22,331 --> 01:36:24,961
(The water is finally boiling.)

2507
01:36:25,271 --> 01:36:27,371
(It's time.)

2508
01:36:28,231 --> 01:36:30,901
(She carries the pig's feet rinsed by Yoon Seo.)

2509
01:36:31,371 --> 01:36:33,771
(Chef Yum looks more nervous than ever.)

2510
01:36:34,071 --> 01:36:36,981
No matter what, I'll make jokbal that doesn't smell bad.

2511
01:36:37,881 --> 01:36:40,511
(The reason Chef Yum is so determined...)

2512
01:36:41,151 --> 01:36:43,981
(The most crucial part of cooking tasty jokbal...)

2513
01:36:44,451 --> 01:36:47,651
(is to remove the pork's strong odour.)

2514
01:36:47,951 --> 01:36:50,661
(Lots of ingredients are needed just to remove the odour.)

2515
01:36:51,121 --> 01:36:53,791
(It's the most challenging dish ever.)

2516
01:36:54,291 --> 01:36:55,601
(Will Jung Ah be able to remove the odour...)

2517
01:36:55,601 --> 01:36:56,931
(and make tasty jokbal?)

2518
01:37:00,431 --> 01:37:02,441
(Pouring soju, which removes the order well)

2519
01:37:03,771 --> 01:37:04,841
We need to remove the foul odour.

2520
01:37:05,841 --> 01:37:08,011
That's the most crucial part. Removing the odour.

2521
01:37:08,011 --> 01:37:09,811
(After pouring a whole bottle of soju, )

2522
01:37:10,311 --> 01:37:12,881
(she places each piece of the chunky pig's feet.)

2523
01:37:14,611 --> 01:37:17,381
(Placing them carefully as if it's a ritual)

2524
01:37:18,081 --> 01:37:19,721
I need to remove the odour today.

2525
01:37:20,691 --> 01:37:21,721
I have to remove it.

2526
01:37:21,721 --> 01:37:22,791
(Vowing to remove the odour for many times)

2527
01:37:23,161 --> 01:37:25,691
(The last piece of the pig's feet is added to the pot.)

2528
01:37:26,031 --> 01:37:27,961
Please don't smell bad.

2529
01:37:27,961 --> 01:37:29,131
(She'll boil it for about 20 minutes.)

2530
01:37:30,661 --> 01:37:31,831
I need to cook the buckwheat noodles.

2531
01:37:32,571 --> 01:37:34,331
No, don't cook the noodles yet.

2532
01:37:34,631 --> 01:37:36,671
Cook noodles last, or they'll get soggy.

2533
01:37:36,941 --> 01:37:39,011
- You can make the sauce now.
- Okay.

2534
01:37:40,411 --> 01:37:42,611
I won't peel the garlic anymore.

2535
01:37:42,881 --> 01:37:43,981
(Thick soy sauce)

2536
01:37:43,981 --> 01:37:45,211
Nine spoonfuls of the thick soy sauce.

2537
01:37:46,051 --> 01:37:47,451
(Yoon Seo pours the soy sauce carefully.)

2538
01:37:47,451 --> 01:37:49,121
Okay. I'm done with garlic.

2539
01:37:49,451 --> 01:37:51,151
(Gushing out)

2540
01:37:51,551 --> 01:37:54,591
(She added about 3 spoonfuls by pouring twice.)

2541
01:37:54,591 --> 01:37:56,461
- Four, five, - Is that enough?

2542
01:37:57,091 --> 01:37:58,361
six,

2543
01:37:59,031 --> 01:38:00,831
seven, eight. Gosh.

2544
01:38:00,831 --> 01:38:02,061
Is this enough?

2545
01:38:02,161 --> 01:38:03,361
(Carefully)

2546
01:38:03,961 --> 01:38:05,031
Nine.

2547
01:38:05,031 --> 01:38:06,201
(Pouring carefully when it's too late)

2548
01:38:06,471 --> 01:38:07,531
Six spoonfuls of the cooking wine.

2549
01:38:08,531 --> 01:38:09,701
Six spoonfuls of vinegar.

2550
01:38:11,241 --> 01:38:12,241
(6 spoonfuls of sugar)

2551
01:38:13,511 --> 01:38:15,941
(Now, it's time to add chilli powder.)

2552
01:38:16,711 --> 01:38:18,711
(She starts pouring the chilli powder.)

2553
01:38:18,711 --> 01:38:19,751
Two,

2554
01:38:20,111 --> 01:38:21,181
three,

2555
01:38:21,181 --> 01:38:22,251
(Pouring while measuring it with her mouth)

2556
01:38:22,251 --> 01:38:23,621
four, five,

2557
01:38:24,851 --> 01:38:25,921
six.

2558
01:38:25,921 --> 01:38:26,921
(Gushing out for the 2nd time)

2559
01:38:28,121 --> 01:38:31,291
(Losing all hope)

2560
01:38:31,721 --> 01:38:33,731
(She doesn't want to believe it.)

2561
01:38:33,991 --> 01:38:35,931
- What happened, Yoon Seo?
- It's nothing.

2562
01:38:35,931 --> 01:38:37,661
- Are you okay? Put it up there.
- I'm okay.

2563
01:38:39,031 --> 01:38:41,931
(She scoops out her mistake in a hurry.)

2564
01:38:42,501 --> 01:38:44,271
(Worried)

2565
01:38:44,971 --> 01:38:46,671
You can make the sauce again.

2566
01:38:47,771 --> 01:38:48,811
It's not a big deal.

2567
01:38:49,111 --> 01:38:50,981
It's okay. I just need to taste it.

2568
01:38:50,981 --> 01:38:52,911
(The youngest sister is positive.)

2569
01:38:55,281 --> 01:38:56,351
(6 spoonfuls of gochujang)

2570
01:38:56,981 --> 01:38:57,981
(Lots of toasted sesame seeds)

2571
01:39:00,451 --> 01:39:02,861
(How will Yoon Seo's sauce taste?)

2572
01:39:08,661 --> 01:39:09,731
Is it good?

2573
01:39:11,431 --> 01:39:12,531
I'm still working on it.

2574
01:39:14,031 --> 01:39:15,671
It needs to be more watery...

2575
01:39:15,671 --> 01:39:17,541
- to mix it with the noodles later.
- Yes.

2576
01:39:17,771 --> 01:39:20,271
(The sauce is way too thick to mix properly.)

2577
01:39:20,511 --> 01:39:22,611
- Want to add some pear drink?
- Yes.

2578
01:39:23,481 --> 01:39:26,481
(Adding pear juice to sweeten it up and thin out the sauce)

2579
01:39:26,881 --> 01:39:28,511
- Gosh.
- It should be more watery.

2580
01:39:28,511 --> 01:39:30,621
- I know.
- How did it taste?

2581
01:39:30,621 --> 01:39:32,421
- It's too salty.
- Too salty?

2582
01:39:33,491 --> 01:39:34,851
Then we should add some more.

2583
01:39:34,851 --> 01:39:35,991
(Adding more)

2584
01:39:36,121 --> 01:39:39,231
(Yoon Seo tastes it again.)

2585
01:39:40,491 --> 01:39:41,791
(Nodding)

2586
01:39:42,161 --> 01:39:45,231
(Humming in surprise)

2587
01:39:45,301 --> 01:39:47,301
Is it delicious? Is it good to go?

2588
01:39:47,301 --> 01:39:48,371
I think it's okay.

2589
01:39:49,341 --> 01:39:51,771
Am I wrong? Could you taste it for me?

2590
01:39:51,771 --> 01:39:53,771
(She goes to get Chef Yum's approval.)

2591
01:39:54,371 --> 01:39:57,211
(Chef Yum tastes it too.)

2592
01:39:57,441 --> 01:40:00,151
(Nervous)

2593
01:40:00,151 --> 01:40:01,411
It tastes good.

2594
01:40:02,481 --> 01:40:03,821
- It's good.
- Is it good?

2595
01:40:03,821 --> 01:40:06,391
- Oh, yes.
- Yes.

2596
01:40:06,621 --> 01:40:08,961
- Success.
- It's a success.

2597
01:40:10,361 --> 01:40:14,431
(Yoon Seo's first makguksu sauce is ready.)

2598
01:40:14,591 --> 01:40:17,161
I'll make some seasoned dried radish.

2599
01:40:18,061 --> 01:40:19,301
Yes, make some seasoned dried radish.

2600
01:40:20,671 --> 01:40:23,071
First, I have to wash dried radish five times.

2601
01:40:23,541 --> 01:40:26,041
(You Seok starts by prepping the dried radish.)

2602
01:40:26,641 --> 01:40:29,841
As you knead and work it with your hands,

2603
01:40:30,141 --> 01:40:33,351
the stiff dried radish gradually becomes soft.

2604
01:40:33,351 --> 01:40:34,751
(Keep soaking and massaging it until it's soft)

2605
01:40:35,081 --> 01:40:36,481
Actually, it's my first time making it...

2606
01:40:37,281 --> 01:40:38,281
so I don't really know.

2607
01:40:38,851 --> 01:40:41,391
(The rookie dried radish cook)

2608
01:40:41,421 --> 01:40:42,861
You Seok, you can do it.

2609
01:40:43,391 --> 01:40:44,991
You can do anything.

2610
01:40:44,991 --> 01:40:46,791
(Auntie Jennica's love for her nephew knows no bounds.)

2611
01:40:47,091 --> 01:40:49,631
(Fuelled by Auntie Jennica's encouragement)

2612
01:40:49,761 --> 01:40:53,071
(He rinses it...)

2613
01:40:53,071 --> 01:40:55,431
(again and again.)

2614
01:40:55,601 --> 01:40:57,471
(After rinsing it again, )

2615
01:40:57,771 --> 01:41:01,871
(he squeezes out the excess water once the dried radish is soaked.)

2616
01:41:02,111 --> 01:41:03,241
Cooking wine?

2617
01:41:04,611 --> 01:41:07,911
I just do it based on my feeling. Turning it once, twice...

2618
01:41:08,481 --> 01:41:09,651
Three times.

2619
01:41:10,081 --> 01:41:12,121
Cooking is all about that personal touch.

2620
01:41:12,121 --> 01:41:13,121
(After giving it roughly three turns)

2621
01:41:13,121 --> 01:41:15,861
I soaked it in cooking wine.

2622
01:41:15,861 --> 01:41:17,361
(Letting it marinate for a while)

2623
01:41:17,861 --> 01:41:20,761
(Meanwhile, the first round of boiling pig's feet is done.)

2624
01:41:20,861 --> 01:41:23,831
(It's time to take it out.)

2625
01:41:24,361 --> 01:41:27,401
(Once you pull it out through the steam)

2626
01:41:28,331 --> 01:41:30,841
(The pig's feet is deliciously cooked.)

2627
01:41:31,671 --> 01:41:32,811
Gosh, it's hot.

2628
01:41:33,571 --> 01:41:36,441
(She plans to boil it again after adding spices.)

2629
01:41:36,541 --> 01:41:38,141
I'll throw it away over there.

2630
01:41:38,141 --> 01:41:40,351
(Jung Ah is about to wash the pot before boiling again.)

2631
01:41:40,351 --> 01:41:41,451
Isn't it heavy?

2632
01:41:42,151 --> 01:41:43,451
(Lifting easily)

2633
01:41:43,451 --> 01:41:45,481
- Move out of the way.
- Over here...

2634
01:41:50,061 --> 01:41:51,921
- What's the matter?
- What is it?

2635
01:41:51,921 --> 01:41:53,291
(You Seok goes running at the sound of an urgent call.)

2636
01:41:53,491 --> 01:41:54,861
My goodness.

2637
01:41:54,861 --> 01:41:57,331
There's a snake!

2638
01:41:57,401 --> 01:41:58,801
(There's a snake.)

2639
01:41:58,801 --> 01:42:01,301
(A snake?)

2640
01:42:01,301 --> 01:42:03,401
- My gosh.
- Where is it?

2641
01:42:03,401 --> 01:42:05,671
- Gosh, there's a snake.
- Where?

2642
01:42:05,811 --> 01:42:07,411
Don't go in there!

2643
01:42:07,971 --> 01:42:10,641
There's a snake. What are you doing?

2644
01:42:11,141 --> 01:42:12,451
- There's a snake.
- Where's the snake?

2645
01:42:12,451 --> 01:42:14,081
Where is it?

2646
01:42:14,081 --> 01:42:15,081
(Where's the snake?)

2647
01:42:15,081 --> 01:42:16,821
Why are you going in there?

2648
01:42:16,951 --> 01:42:18,951
Where is it?

2649
01:42:19,521 --> 01:42:21,121
- Hey.
- There's a snake.

2650
01:42:21,151 --> 01:42:23,461
It's dangerous. Don't go there.

2651
01:42:23,461 --> 01:42:24,861
- Hey.
- There's a snake.

2652
01:42:24,861 --> 01:42:26,491
(What do we do?)

2653
01:42:26,731 --> 01:42:28,061
- Hey.
- You Seok.

2654
01:42:28,061 --> 01:42:29,461
Get out of there, You Seok.

2655
01:42:29,461 --> 01:42:30,931
What is he doing?

2656
01:42:31,801 --> 01:42:34,771
(Worried about You Seok, Yoon Seo also goes inside.)

2657
01:42:34,771 --> 01:42:36,301
Oh, no. You Seok.

2658
01:42:36,301 --> 01:42:38,041
You Seok, come back here.

2659
01:42:38,041 --> 01:42:40,071
You can't use that. No way.

2660
01:42:40,071 --> 01:42:41,211
- What's wrong with you?
- Gosh.

2661
01:42:42,841 --> 01:42:43,941
What happened?

2662
01:42:46,688 --> 01:42:48,788
(A mission given to Chef Yum for tonight's dinner)

2663
01:42:49,088 --> 01:42:51,758
(Make jokbal!)

2664
01:42:52,318 --> 01:42:55,558
(The siblings' best dish is born.)

2665
01:42:55,558 --> 01:42:58,558
(Featuring all handmade garlic sauce)

2666
01:42:58,628 --> 01:42:59,998
(A taste so incredible you'll question your own tongue)

2667
01:43:00,028 --> 01:43:01,728
(Chewy like jelly)

2668
01:43:02,128 --> 01:43:04,698
(An especially bittersweet night in Taean)

2669
01:43:05,298 --> 01:43:06,568
(Every day was eventful.)

2670
01:43:08,008 --> 01:43:11,638
(The events aren't over yet.)

2671
01:43:11,938 --> 01:43:13,048
(Did the production crew do it again?)

2672
01:43:13,048 --> 01:43:14,408
(What's wrong with them?)

2673
01:43:15,108 --> 01:43:16,678
(Did the siblings get owned?)

2674
01:43:16,678 --> 01:43:17,878
(Yoon Seo, the optimistic girl)

2675
01:43:17,878 --> 01:43:19,948
(She shows her dark side.)

2676
01:43:19,948 --> 01:43:21,818
(Your opponent is chickens.)

2677
01:43:21,988 --> 01:43:23,088
(Gasping)

2678
01:43:23,488 --> 01:43:24,518
(Horrified)

2679
01:43:24,658 --> 01:43:26,628
(A showdown with chickens in its raw form)

2680
01:43:27,358 --> 01:43:29,758
(Meanwhile, Sun Young begins a battle of her own.)

2681
01:43:29,828 --> 01:43:30,958
Isn't it too thick?

2682
01:43:30,958 --> 01:43:32,058
(Anxiety)

2683
01:43:32,058 --> 01:43:33,228
(Lack of confidence)

2684
01:43:33,628 --> 01:43:36,798
(I still want to please Jung Ah.)

2685
01:43:36,898 --> 01:43:39,408
(A morning without Captain Yum equals...)

2686
01:43:39,408 --> 01:43:40,968
(a disaster.)

2687
01:43:41,508 --> 01:43:45,208
(How will the loudest morning at the siblings' end?)
